1. Introduction to CSS Grid
CSS Grid is a two-dimensional layout system (rows and columns).
Full HTML Example:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container { display: grid; }
.box { background: lightblue; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


2. grid-template-columns
Defines number and size of columns.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
}
.box { background: lightcoral; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
  <div class="box">3</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


3. grid-template-rows
Defines row heights.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 100px 200px;
}
.box { background: lightgreen; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">Row1</div>
  <div class="box">Row2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


4. gap
Adds spacing between grid items.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr);
  gap: 20px;
}
.box { background: orange; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
  <div class="box">3</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


5. grid-column & grid-row
Controls spanning across columns/rows.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr);
}
.box1 { grid-column: span 2; background: lightblue; }
.box { background: pink; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box1">Span 2 cols</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
  <div class="box">3</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


6. justify-items & align-items
Align items inside each cell.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  height:200px;
  justify-items: center;
  align-items: center;
}
.box { background: purple; color:white; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">Centered</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


7. justify-content & align-content
Align the whole grid inside container.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 100px 100px;
  height:200px;
  justify-content: center;
  align-content: center;
}
.box { background: teal; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


8. auto-fit with minmax
Creates responsive grid that stretches items.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(100px,1fr));
  gap:10px;
}
.box { background: skyblue; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
  <div class="box">3</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


9. auto-fill
Creates columns even if empty.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(100px,1fr));
  gap:10px;
}
.box { background: salmon; padding:20px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="box">1</div>
  <div class="box">2</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>


10. grid-template-areas
Defines layout using named areas.
Full HTML Example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
.container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header header"
    "sidebar main";
}
.header { grid-area: header; background:lightblue; }
.sidebar { grid-area: sidebar; background:lightgreen; }
.main { grid-area: main; background:lightcoral; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="header">Header</div>
  <div class="sidebar">Sidebar</div>
  <div class="main">Main</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
